urname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Salmon</surname><given-names>E.D.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Force generation by microtubule assembly/disassembly in mitosis and related movements</article-title><source>Mol. Biol. Cell.</source><volume>6</volume><year>1995</year><fpage>1619</fpage><lpage>1640</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8590794</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Jankeetal2001"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Janke</surname><given-names>C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Ortiz</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Lechner</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Shevchenko</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Shevchenko</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Magiera</surname><given-names>M.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Schramm</surname><given-names>C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Schiebel</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The budding yeast proteins Spc24p and Spc25p interact with Ndc80p and Nuf2p at the kinetochore and are important for kinetochore clustering and checkpoint control</article-title><source>EMBO (Eur. Mol. Biol. Organ.).</source><volume>20</volume><year>2001</year><fpage>777</fpage><lpage>791</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="Kahanaetal1995"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kahana</surname><given-names>J.A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Schnapp</surname><given-names>B.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Silver</surname><given-names>P.A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Kinetics of spindle pole body separation in budding yeast</article-title><source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source><volume>92</volume><year>1995</year><fpage>9707</fpage><lpage>9711</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7568202</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="KhodjakovandRieder1996"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Khodjakov</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Rieder</surname><given-names>C.L.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Kinetochores moving away from their associated pole do not exert a significant pushing force on the chromosome</article-title><source>J. Cell Biol</source><volume>135</volume><year>1996</year><fpage>315</fpage><lpage>327</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8896591</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Kubai1975"><citation citation-type="other">Kubai, D.F. 1975. Mitosis and fungal phylogeny. Nuclear Division in the Fungi. I.B. Heath, editor. 177&#x02013;229.</citation></ref><ref id="Maddoxetal2000"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Maddox</surname><given-names>P.</given-names></name><name><surname>Bloom</surname><given-names>K.</given-names></name><name><surname>Salmon</surname><given-names>E.D.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Polarity and dynamics of microtubule assembly in the budding yeast <italic>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</italic></article-title><source>Nat. Cell Biol.</source><volume>2</volume><year>2000</year><fpage>36</fpage><lpage>41</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10620805</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Maneyetal2000"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Maney</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Ginkel</surname><given-names>L.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Hunter</surname><given-names>A.W.</given-names></name><name><surname>Wordeman</surname><given-names>L.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The kinetochore of higher eucaryotesa molecular view</article-title><source>Int. Rev. Cyt.</source><volume>194</volume><year>2000</year><fpage>67</fpage><lpage>131</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="McIntosh1991"><citation citation-type="journ