>Arana</surname><given-names>P.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evolution and the meaning of metaphase</article-title><source>J. Cell Sci.</source><volume>102</volume><year>1992</year><fpage>681</fpage><lpage>690</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1429886</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="NicklasandKoch1969"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nicklas</surname><given-names>R.B.</given-names></name><name><surname>Koch</surname><given-names>C.A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Chromosome micromanipulation III. Spindle fiber tension and the reorientation of mal-oriented chromosomes</article-title><source>J. Cell Biol.</source><volume>43</volume><year>1969</year><fpage>40</fpage><lpage>50</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5824068</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Osborneetal1994"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Osborne</surname><given-names>M.A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Schlenstedt</surname><given-names>G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Jinks</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Silver</surname><given-names>P.A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nuf2, a spindle pole body-associated protein required for nuclear division in yeast</article-title><source>J. Cell Biol.</source><volume>125</volume><year>1994</year><fpage>853</fpage><lpage>866</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8188751</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="OTooleandWiney2001"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>O'Toole</surname><given-names>E.T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Winey</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The spindle cycle in budding yeast</article-title><source>Nat. Cell Biol.</source><volume>3</volume><year>2001</year><fpage>E23</fpage><lpage>E27</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11146646</pub-id></citation></